LLVM C++ runtime — libc++, libc++abi, libunwind — version 18.1.8
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
License:  Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
          (SPDX: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception)
Upstream: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project (libcxx, libcxxabi, libunwind)
Verified against the LLVM Project LICENSE.TXT of release 18.1.8 (the
"Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions" header and "LLVM Exceptions to the
Apache 2.0 License" section; read from the conda libllvm 18.1.8 package's
copy on the build box). Baked into the Linux shared library
(liboverlume.so, which statically links libc++.a, libc++abi.a and
libunwind.a from the official LLVM 18.1.8 release tarball, see
overlume/cmake/toolchain-llvm-release.cmake) so consumers need no libc++.
The Linux static package leaves them out (the consumer's own libc++ is used).
Android binaries statically link the NDK r27c libc++ (c++_static, same
license; NDK distribution, https://developer.android.com/ndk). macOS and iOS
link the system libc++ dynamically (not redistributed). Windows ships the
MSVC redistributable (vcruntime140*.dll, msvcp140*.dll) app-local beside
overlume.dll under the Microsoft Visual C++ redistributable terms.

